<blockquote class="uncited"><div>On my Tytera UV-MD390 and 380 radios APRS behaves as described by Daniel: <em class="text-italics">When any mode is selected, except PTT (which uses SK1 + 2 to trigger beaconing), you can just change to the next/previous channel, then come back to the original channel, that will send a beacon.</em><br>With the Tytera 9600 even though the GPS has acquired the position and the channel settings are correct this does not happen, the APRS beacon does not start when changing channels, in fact: it does not start at all, is it possible that I made a mistake in the configuration? Yet the code plug is basically the same.....</div></blockquote>My MD-9600 V2 transmit the aprs packets , I disabled decay as I'm at a fixed location and it transmit at 1 minute as I configured it.<br>A short interruption is heard when 434.025 is active. <br><div class="codebox"><p>CODE: </p><pre><code>2025-01-22 09:57:07 CET: SA0BUX-9&gt;APOG77,WIDE1-1,WIDE2-1,qAR,SM0RGQ-4:!\0OunS%X-C  !434.025MHz C077 +000 OpenGD77 MD-96002025-01-22 09:58:08 CET: SA0BUX-9&gt;APOG77,SK0VR-2,WIDE1*,WIDE2-1,qAR,SK0BJ-10:!\0OufS%X,C  !434.025MHz C077 +000 OpenGD77 MD-96002025-01-22 10:00:07 CET: SA0BUX-9&gt;APOG77,WIDE1-1,WIDE2-1,qAR,SM0RGQ-4:!\0Ou0S%X%C  !434.025MHz C077 +000 OpenGD77 MD-96002025-01-22 10:01:07 CET: SA0BUX-9&gt;APOG77,WIDE1-1,WIDE2-1,qAR,SM0RGQ-4:!\0OuFS%X!C  !434.025MHz C077 +000 OpenGD77 MD-96002025-01-22 10:02:07 CET: SA0BUX-9&gt;APOG77,WIDE1-1,WIDE2-1,qAR,SM0RGQ-4:!\0OuMS%WzC  !434.025MHz C077 +000 OpenGD77 MD-9600</code></pre></div><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Wed Jan 22, 2025 9:06 am</p><hr />
